    "prompt": "For any matrix $M \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$ with Moore-Penrose pseudoinverse $M^\\dagger$, the matrices $M M^\\dagger \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times m}$ and $M^\\dagger M \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times n}$ are always symmetric and idempotent (i.e., $(MM^\\dagger)^\\top = MM^\\dagger$ and $(MM^\\dagger)^2 = MM^\\dagger$), even when $M$ is rank-deficient.",
