    "roundingNote": null,
    "correctedStatement": null,
    "distractorExplanations": null,
    "explanation": "True. Using the compact SVD $M = U\\Sigma V^\\top$ and $M^\\dagger = V\\Sigma^{-1}U^\\top$ (`ESI.pdf`, p. 7 Problem 3a), we have $M M^\\dagger = U\\Sigma V^\\top V\\Sigma^{-1}U^\\top = U U^\\top$ and $M^\\dagger M = V\\Sigma^{-1}U^\\top U\\Sigma V^\\top = V V^\\top$. Both $U U^\\top$ and $V V^\\top$ are clearly symmetric, and $(MM^\\dagger)(MM^\\dagger) = (MM^\\dagger M)M^\\dagger = M M^\\dagger$, so they are orthogonal projection matrices (and consequently $I - M^\\dagger M$ is also an orthogonal projection matrix, like $\\Pi = I - U^\\dagger U$ in subspace identification)."
