    "prompt": "For an estimator $\\hat{\\theta}$ of a true parameter vector $\\theta_o \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$, define: (1) Bias and unbiasedness, (2) Covariance matrix $\\text{Cov}(\\hat{\\theta})$ and the meaning of its diagonal/off-diagonal entries, (3) Mean Squared Error $\\text{MSE}(\\hat{\\theta})$ and its bias-variance decomposition, and (4) Consistency as $N \\to \\infty$.",
    "hint": "Review the four definition boxes on pages 11-12 and Appendix B (p. 19) of `LinReg2021.pdf`.",
    "options": null,
    "correctAnswer": "1. Bias (`LinReg2021.pdf` p. 11): $\\text{Bias}(\\hat{\\theta}) = \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{\\theta}] - \\theta_o \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$. The estimator is unbiased if $\\text{Bias}(\\hat{\\theta}) = 0$, i.e., $\\mathbb{E}[\\hat{\\theta}] = \\theta_o$ (for a given finite $N$). It is asymptotically unbiased if $\\mathbb{E}[\\hat{\\theta}(N)] \\to \\theta_o$ as $N \\to \\infty$.\n\n2. Covariance matrix (`LinReg2021.pdf` p. 11): $\\text{Cov}(\\hat{\\theta}) = \\mathbb{E}[(\\hat{\\theta} - \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{\\theta}])(\\hat{\\theta} - \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{\\theta}])^\\top] \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times d}$. It is a symmetric positive semidefinite $d \\times d$ matrix where the $i$-th diagonal entry is the variance $\\text{Var}(\\hat{\\theta}_i)$ and the $(i,j)$-th off-diagonal entry is the cross-covariance between $\\hat{\\theta}_i$ and $\\hat{\\theta}_j$.\n\n3. Mean Squared Error (`LinReg2021.pdf` p. 11): $\\text{MSE}(\\hat{\\theta}) = \\mathbb{E}[\\|\\hat{\\theta} - \\theta_o\\|_2^2] = \\|\\text{Bias}(\\hat{\\theta})\\|_2^2 + \\text{tr}(\\text{Cov}(\\hat{\\theta}))$ (for a scalar parameter, $\\text{MSE} = b^2 + v$).\n\n4. Consistency (`LinReg2021.pdf` p. 12 & p. 19): $\\hat{\\theta}(N)$ is consistent if $\\hat{\\theta}(N) \\to \\theta_o$ as $N \\to \\infty$ (or in mean square, $\\text{MSE}(\\hat{\\theta}(N)) = \\mathbb{E}[\\|\\hat{\\theta}(N) - \\theta_o\\|_2^2] \\to 0$ as $N \\to \\infty$, which happens iff both the bias and the variance go to zero as $N \\to \\infty$).",
