    "explanation": "This asymptotic analysis (`LinReg2021.pdf` Section 3.2, pp. 14-15; `L13.pdf` slides 22-23/25) explains the simulation plots in Lecture 1 (`L1.pdf` slides 26-27/30): ARX least squares converges to the true parameters when the disturbance $w(t) = e(t)$ is white noise, but converges to biased parameter values when $w(t)$ is colored noise."
