    "prompt": "Consider the true system $y(t) = b_o u(t) + e(t)$ with $b_o = 5$, where $u(t)$ is zero-mean white noise with variance $\\sigma_u^2 = 4$ and $e(t)$ is zero-mean white noise with variance $\\sigma_e^2 = 1$. The input is measured with noise: $u_m(t) = u(t) + v(t)$, where $v(t)$ is zero-mean white noise with variance $\\sigma_v^2 = 1$. Assume $u(t)$, $e(t)$, and $v(t)$ are mutually uncorrelated. If we estimate $b$ by linear least squares using the model $\\hat{y}(t) = b u_m(t)$, what value does $\\hat{b}$ converge to as $N \\to \\infty$?",
    "hint": "As $N \\to \\infty$, $\\hat{b} \\to (\\mathbb{E}[u_m^2(t)])^{-1} \\mathbb{E}[u_m(t)y(t)]$. Compute $\\mathbb{E}[u_m^2(t)] = \\sigma_u^2 + \\sigma_v^2$ and $\\mathbb{E}[u_m(t)y(t)] = b_o \\sigma_u^2$. See `SI_rexam2020.pdf` Problem 5 (p. 7).",
