    "prompt": "Suppose the true system is $y(t) + a_1^o y(t-1) + a_2^o y(t-2) = b_1^o u(t-1) + b_2^o u(t-2) + w(t)$, where the input $u(t)$ is persistently exciting and independent of the disturbance $w(t)$, but $w(t)$ is zero-mean COLORED noise ($R_w(1) \\ne 0$). Then estimating an ARX predictor $\\hat{y}(t) = -a_1 y(t-1) - a_2 y(t-2) + b_1 u(t-1) + b_2 u(t-2)$ by least squares yields biased (inconsistent) parameter estimates as $N \\to \\infty$, whereas using an Output-Error (OE) predictor $\\hat{y}(t) = -a_1 \\hat{y}(t-1) - a_2 \\hat{y}(t-2) + b_1 u(t-1) + b_2 u(t-2)$ yields consistent estimates.",
