    "prompt": "In the linear model structure $y(t) = \\frac{b_1 q^{-1}}{a_0 + a_1 q^{-1}} u(t) + e(t)$, if $a_0$, $a_1$, and $b_1$ are all treated as free parameters to be estimated simultaneously, the parametrization is uniquely identifiable provided that the input $u(t)$ is white noise.",
    "hint": "Check what happens to the transfer function $G(q) = \\frac{b_1 q^{-1}}{a_0 + a_1 q^{-1}}$ if you multiply all three parameters $a_0, a_1, b_1$ by an arbitrary non-zero constant $c$.",
