    "prompt": "The exponential smoothing predictor is given by\n$$\\hat{y}(t) = \\frac{(1 - \\alpha)q^{-1}}{1 - \\alpha q^{-1}}y(t)$$\nwhere $|\\alpha| < 1$. For which ARMA process $A(q)y(t) = C(q)e(t)$ (where $e(t)$ is zero-mean white noise) is this the optimal 1-step-ahead predictor?",
    "hint": "For a pure signal model $y(t) = H(q)e(t) = \\frac{C(q)}{A(q)}e(t)$ with $G(q) = 0$, the optimal 1-step predictor is $\\hat{y}(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{A(q)}{C(q)}\\right)y(t) = \\frac{C(q) - A(q)}{C(q)}y(t)$. Match the numerator and monic denominator polynomials.",
