    "prompt": "In the general linear model $y(t) = G(q)u(t) + H(q)e(t)$, the normalization $H(\\infty) = 1$ (meaning the leading constant term of both $C(q)$ and $D(q)$ in $q^{-1}$ is $1$) ensures that the filter $1 - \\frac{1}{H(q)}$ contains a factor $q^{-1}$, so that $\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{H(q)}\\right)y(t)$ depends only on past measurements $y(t-1), y(t-2), \\dots$ and not on $y(t)$.",
    "hint": "Expand $1 - \\frac{D(q)}{C(q)} = \\frac{C(q) - D(q)}{C(q)}$ when $C(q) = 1 + c_1 q^{-1} + \\dots$ and $D(q) = 1 + d_1 q^{-1} + \\dots$.",
