    "prompt": "Consider the FIR system $y(t) = K u(t-1) + v(t)$, where the input $u(t)$ is deterministic (or generated in open loop completely independently of $v$) and $\\sum_{t=1}^N u^2(t-1) > 0$. If $K$ is estimated using ordinary linear least squares, the estimator $\\hat{K}$ is unbiased ($\\mathbb{E}[\\hat{K}] = K$) even if the disturbance $v(t)$ is coloured (autocorrelated) noise, as long as $\\mathbb{E}[v(t)] = 0$ for all $t$.",
    "hint": "Check Theorem 2 in the Linear Regression compendium: what assumptions on the noise vector $v$ are used to prove $\\mathbb{E}[\\hat{\\theta} - \\theta_0] = \\mathbb{E}[(\\Phi^\\top \\Phi)^{-1} \\Phi^\\top v] = 0$ when $\\Phi$ is deterministic/independent of $v$?",
    "options": null,
