    "explanation": "As $N \\to \\infty$, the linear least-squares estimate converges to:\n$$\\hat{\\theta} \\to \\theta_0 + \\mathbb{E}[\\varphi(t)\\varphi^\\top(t)]^{-1} \\mathbb{E}[\\varphi(t)w(t)]$$\nAssuming $\\mathbb{E}[\\varphi(t)\\varphi^\\top(t)]$ is invertible, consistency requires $\\mathbb{E}[\\varphi(t)w(t)] = 0$:\n- **System 1 (FIR):** $\\varphi_1(t) = [u(t-1) \\;\\; u(t-2)]^\\top$. Because $u$ and $w$ are independent with zero mean, $\\mathbb{E}[u(t-1)w(t)] = \\mathbb{E}[u(t-2)w(t)] = 0$ regardless of whether $w(t)$ is white or coloured! Thus LS is **consistent**.\n- **System 2:** $\\varphi_2(t) = [-y(t-1) \\;\\; u(t-1)]^\\top$. Here $y(t-1) = -a_o y(t-2) + b_o u(t-2) + e(t-1) + c_1 e(t-2)$ depends on $e(t-1)$, and $w(t) = e(t) + c_1 e(t-1)$ also depends on $e(t-1)$. Therefore, $\\mathbb{E}[y(t-1)w(t)] = c_1 \\lambda_e \\neq 0$, so $\\mathbb{E}[\\varphi_2(t)w(t)] \\neq 0$ and LS is **inconsistent**."
