    "explanation": "On Slide 19/22 of Lecture 7, the large-sample variance of the estimated transfer function in the frequency domain is given by:\n$$\\text{Var}\\left(G(e^{i\\omega}; \\hat{\\theta})\\right) \\approx \\frac{n}{N} \\frac{\\lambda}{\\Phi_u(\\omega)}$$\nwhere $n$ is the model order (number of estimated parameters), $N$ is the number of data samples, $\\lambda$ is the noise variance, and $\\Phi_u(\\omega)$ is the input spectrum.\n- **Lower model order $n \\implies$ lower variance** (fewer parameters to estimate from the same $N$ data points), though choosing $n$ too small introduces **bias** (underfitting).\n- **Higher model order $n \\implies$ higher variance** (overfitting)."
