    "prompt": "Suppose $Y = \\Phi^\\top \\theta + e$ where $\\Phi^\\top \\in \\mathbb{R}^{N \\times d}$ is deterministic and the Gaussian noise vector has a known non-scalar positive definite covariance matrix $e \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, R_e)$ with $R_e \\neq \\lambda I_N$. What is the Maximum Likelihood estimator $\\hat{\\theta}_{\\text{ML}}$?",
    "hint": "Write the quadratic form in the exponent of the multivariate normal density $p(Y; \\theta) = ((2\\pi)^N \\det R_e)^{-1/2} \\exp\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}(Y - \\Phi^\\top \\theta)^\\top R_e^{-1}(Y - \\Phi^\\top \\theta)\\right)$ and minimize it with respect to $\\theta$.",
