    "prompt": "Consider the first-order ARX system $y(t) + a y(t-1) = b u(t-1) + e(t)$ with i.i.d. Gaussian noise $e(t) \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, \\lambda)$ and fixed initial conditions. Suppose the Maximum Likelihood (and PEM/LS) parameter estimates from a dataset are $\\hat{a} = -0.6$ and $\\hat{b} = 1.2$. By the invariance principle of Maximum Likelihood estimation, what is the Maximum Likelihood estimate of the system's static (DC) gain $K_{\\text{DC}} = G(1; \\theta) = \\frac{b}{1 + a}$?",
