    "prompt": "When the true system belongs to the model set ($\\theta_o \\in \\mathcal{M}$) and the innovations $e(t) \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, \\lambda)$ are i.i.d. Gaussian white noise, the PEM estimator (which coincides with the ML estimator) is asymptotically efficient, meaning its asymptotic covariance matrix $\\frac{\\lambda}{N} \\bar{R}^{-1}$ achieves the Cramér-Rao lower bound as $N \\to \\infty$.",
    "hint": "Recall the asymptotic optimality properties of Maximum Likelihood and PEM when the innovation distribution is Gaussian.",
    "options": null,
    "correctAnswer": true,
    "tolerance": null,
