    "roundingNote": null,
    "correctedStatement": null,
    "distractorExplanations": null,
    "explanation": "Under Gaussian innovations $e(t) \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, \\lambda)$ and correct model specification, the PEM estimator is the Maximum Likelihood estimator. By the asymptotic efficiency of ML, as $N \\to \\infty$, $\\sqrt{N}(\\hat{\\theta}_N - \\theta_o) \\xrightarrow{d} \\mathcal{N}(0, \\lambda \\bar{R}^{-1})$, where $\\bar{R} = \\mathbb{E}[\\psi(t, \\theta_o)\\psi^\\top(t, \\theta_o)]$ with $\\psi(t, \\theta) = \\frac{d}{d\\theta}\\hat{y}(t|\\theta)$. Here $\\frac{N}{\\lambda}\\bar{R}$ is the asymptotic Fisher information matrix, so $\\text{cov}(\\hat{\\theta}_N) \\approx \\frac{\\lambda}{N}\\bar{R}^{-1}$ attains the Cramér-Rao lower bound."
