    "explanation": "For an OE model, $H(q; \\theta) = 1$, so the optimal 1-step-ahead predictor is $\\hat{y}(t|\\theta) = \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{1}\\right)y(t) + \\frac{G(q;\\theta)}{1}u(t) = G(q; \\theta)u(t)$. Since $\\hat{y}(t|\\theta)$ depends only on the input sequence $u(t)$ and not on past measured outputs $y(t)$, 1-step prediction and simulation coincide. Furthermore, because $\\varepsilon(t, \\theta) = y(t) - \\frac{B(q)}{F(q)}u(t)$ is rational in the coefficients of $F(q)$, nonlinear optimization is required."
