    "prompt": "Suppose the true data-generating system is $y(t) = G_o(q)u(t) + w(t)$. Before fitting a model, we filter both the input and the output through the same linear time-invariant filter $L(q)$, defining $u_F(t) = L(q)u(t)$ and $y_F(t) = L(q)y(t)$. What is the effect of using $(u_F(t), y_F(t))$ for identification?",
