    "prompt": "In `ESI.pdf` Exercise 4, we minimize $V(\\Theta) = \\text{tr}\\left\\{(\\mathbf{Y} - \\Theta\\mathbf{\\Phi})^\\top(\\mathbf{Y} - \\Theta\\mathbf{\\Phi})\\right\\}$ where $\\mathbf{Y} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{(n+p) \\times N}$, $\\Theta \\in \\mathbb{R}^{(n+p) \\times (n+m)}$, and $\\mathbf{\\Phi} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{(n+m) \\times N}$. Why is the general family of minimizers written as\n$$\\widehat{\\Theta} = \\mathbf{Y}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\dagger + \\mathbf{W}(I - \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\dagger)$$\nfor any $\\mathbf{W} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{(n+p) \\times (n+m)}$, with $I - \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\dagger$ rather than $I - \\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\dagger\\mathbf{\\Phi}$?",
    "hint": "Check the dimension of $I - \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\dagger$ and what happens when you multiply $\\widehat{\\Theta}$ on the right by $\\mathbf{\\Phi}$.",
