    "prompt": "In the subspace identification data equation $\\mathbf{Y} = \\mathcal{O}_r X + \\mathcal{T}_r \\mathbf{U} + M$, where $\\mathbf{U} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{mr \\times N}$ has full row rank ($mr$), we multiply from the right by the projection matrix\n$$\\Pi = I - \\mathbf{U}^\\dagger \\mathbf{U} = I - \\mathbf{U}^\\top(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1}\\mathbf{U}.$$\nWhat is the exact algebraic effect of multiplying $\\mathbf{Y}$ from the right by $\\Pi$?",
    "hint": "Compute $\\mathbf{U}\\Pi = \\mathbf{U}(I - \\mathbf{U}^\\dagger \\mathbf{U})$ using the first Moore-Penrose identity $\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\dagger\\mathbf{U} = \\mathbf{U}$.",
