    "prompt": "Given that $\\mathbf{U} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{mr \\times N}$ has full row rank ($mr$) and the LQ-factorization is\n$$\\begin{bmatrix} \\mathbf{U} \\\\ \\mathbf{Y} \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} L_{11} & 0 \\\\ L_{21} & L_{22} \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} Q_1^\\top \\\\ Q_2^\\top \\end{bmatrix}$$\nwith $Q_1^\\top Q_1 = I$, $Q_2^\\top Q_2 = I$, and $Q_1^\\top Q_2 = 0$, prove step-by-step that $G = \\mathbf{Y}\\Pi = \\mathbf{Y}(I - \\mathbf{U}^\\top(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1}\\mathbf{U}) = L_{22}Q_2^\\top$.",
    "hint": "Write $\\mathbf{U} = L_{11}Q_1^\\top$, compute $\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top = L_{11}L_{11}^\\top$, simplify $\\mathbf{U}^\\dagger\\mathbf{U} = Q_1 Q_1^\\top$, and expand $\\mathbf{Y}(I - Q_1 Q_1^\\top)$.",
