    "explanation": "Full derivation from `ESI.pdf` pages 8–9 (Solution 5):\n1. From the top block of the LQ factorization, $\\mathbf{U} = L_{11}Q_1^\\top$. Using $Q_1^\\top Q_1 = I$, we get $\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top = L_{11}Q_1^\\top Q_1 L_{11}^\\top = L_{11}L_{11}^\\top$.\n2. Since $\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top$ is invertible, $L_{11}$ is invertible and $(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1} = (L_{11}^\\top)^{-1}L_{11}^{-1}$.\n3. Thus $\\mathbf{U}^\\dagger\\mathbf{U} = \\mathbf{U}^\\top(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1}\\mathbf{U} = Q_1 L_{11}^\\top (L_{11}^\\top)^{-1} L_{11}^{-1} L_{11} Q_1^\\top = Q_1 Q_1^\\top$.\n4. Substituting $\\mathbf{Y} = L_{21}Q_1^\\top + L_{22}Q_2^\\top$ and $\\Pi = I - Q_1 Q_1^\\top$, and using $Q_1^\\top Q_1 = I, Q_2^\\top Q_1 = 0$, gives:\n$$G = (L_{21}Q_1^\\top + L_{22}Q_2^\\top)(I - Q_1 Q_1^\\top) = L_{22}Q_2^\\top.$$"
