    "explanation": "From `ESI.pdf` page 9 (Solution 6):\nLetting $M = \\begin{bmatrix} \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top & \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\mathbf{U}^\\top \\\\ \\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top & \\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top \\end{bmatrix}^{-1} = \\begin{bmatrix} M_{11} & M_{12} \\\\ M_{21} & M_{22} \\end{bmatrix}$, the Schur complement of $\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top$ is:\n$$\\Delta = \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top - \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\mathbf{U}^\\top(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1}\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top = \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\left(I - \\mathbf{U}^\\top(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1}\\mathbf{U}\\right)\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top = \\mathbf{\\Phi}\\Pi\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top.$$\nBy the block matrix inversion lemma, $M_{11} = \\Delta^{-1} = (\\mathbf{\\Phi}\\Pi\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top)^{-1}$ and $M_{21} = -(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1}\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top(\\mathbf{\\Phi}\\Pi\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top)^{-1}$, which yields:\n$$\\widehat{\\Theta} = \\mathbf{Y}\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top M_{11} + \\mathbf{Y}\\mathbf{U}^\\top M_{21} = \\mathbf{Y}\\left(I - \\mathbf{U}^\\top(\\mathbf{U}\\mathbf{U}^\\top)^{-1}\\mathbf{U}\\right)\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top(\\mathbf{\\Phi}\\Pi\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top)^{-1} = \\mathbf{Y}\\Pi\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top(\\mathbf{\\Phi}\\Pi\\mathbf{\\Phi}^\\top)^{-1} = \\mathbf{Y}\\Pi(\\mathbf{\\Phi}\\Pi)^\\dagger.$$"
