    "prompt": "In subspace identification, the column space of $\\hat{G}$ only determines the extended observability matrix $\\mathcal{O}_r$ up to right-multiplication by an unknown invertible $n \\times n$ state-basis transformation matrix $T$, i.e., $\\mathcal{O}_r T = \\begin{bmatrix} CT \\\\ CAT \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ CA^{r-1}T \\end{bmatrix}$, which yields the similarity-transformed state matrix $\\hat{A} = T^{-1}AT$. Why is the scalar parameter $a$ in a first-order system ($n = 1$) nevertheless **uniquely** determined by the range space of $\\mathcal{O}_2 = \\begin{bmatrix} c \\\\ ca \\end{bmatrix}$?",
