    "explanation": "Using $\\mathbf{X}^\\top\\mathbf{X} = \\mathbf{I}_p$ and $\\widehat{\\boldsymbol{\\theta}}^{\\text{LS}} = \\mathbf{X}^\\top\\mathbf{y}$:\n$$\\|\\mathbf{y} - \\mathbf{X}\\boldsymbol{\\theta}\\|_2^2 + \\lambda\\|\\boldsymbol{\\theta}\\|_1 = \\|\\mathbf{y}\\|_2^2 - \\|\\widehat{\\boldsymbol{\\theta}}^{\\text{LS}}\\|_2^2 + \\sum_{j=1}^p \\left[(\\theta_j - \\widehat{\\theta}_j^{\\text{LS}})^2 + \\lambda|\\theta_j|\\right].$$\nMinimizing $\\phi(\\theta_j) = (\\theta_j - a)^2 + \\lambda|\\theta_j|$ where $a = \\widehat{\\theta}_j^{\\text{LS}}$:\n- For $\\theta_j > 0$: $\\phi'(\\theta_j) = 2(\\theta_j - a) + \\lambda = 0 \\implies \\theta_j = a - \\lambda/2$, which is feasible ($\\theta_j > 0$) iff $a > \\lambda/2$.\n- For $\\theta_j < 0$: $\\phi'(\\theta_j) = 2(\\theta_j - a) - \\lambda = 0 \\implies \\theta_j = a + \\lambda/2$, which is feasible ($\\theta_j < 0$) iff $a < -\\lambda/2$.\n- For $|a| \\le \\lambda/2$: the minimizer is $\\theta_j = 0$.\nCombining all three cases gives the soft-thresholding operator $\\widehat{\\theta}_j^{\\text{Lasso}} = \\operatorname{sign}(\\widehat{\\theta}_j^{\\text{LS}})\\left(|\\widehat{\\theta}_j^{\\text{LS}}| - \\frac{\\lambda}{2}\\right)_+$."
