    "prompt": "When using hold-out cross-validation to tune the regularization parameter $\\gamma$ (or model order) for a dynamical system $y(t) = G(q)u(t) + e(t)$ with $N = 100$ sequential time-series samples, a good way to split the data into two equal non-overlapping sets is to use the odd time indices $(y(1), u(1)), (y(3), u(3)), \\dots, (y(99), u(99))$ for estimation and the even time indices $(y(2), u(2)), (y(4), u(4)), \\dots, (y(100), u(100))$ for validation.",
