    "prompt": "Consider estimating a time-varying mean $y(t) = \\theta + e(t)$ (where $\\varphi(t) = 1$) using RLS with a forgetting factor $\\lambda \\in (0, 1)$. The recursive update is\n$$\\hat{\\theta}(t) = \\hat{\\theta}(t-1) + K(t)\\left(y(t) - \\hat{\\theta}(t-1)\\right), \\quad K(t) = \\frac{1}{\\sum_{k=1}^t \\lambda^{t-k}}.$$\nIf the forgetting factor is set to $\\lambda = 0.96$, what value does the gain $K(t)$ converge to as $t \\to \\infty$?",
    "hint": "Use the geometric series $\\sum_{k=1}^t \\lambda^{t-k} = 1 + \\lambda + \\dots + \\lambda^{t-1} \\to \\frac{1}{1 - \\lambda}$ as $t \\to \\infty$ for $0 < \\lambda < 1$.",
    "options": null,
