    "prompt": "Data is generated from the FIR(2) system $y(t) = b_1^o u(t) + b_2^o u(t-1) + e(t)$ ($\\mathbb{E}[e(t)] = 0$, $\\operatorname{Var}(e(t)) = \\sigma^2 = 1$ white noise) using a unit step input $u(t) = 0$ for $t \\le 0$ and $u(t) = 1$ for $t = 1, \\dots, N$. The regressor is $\\varphi(1) = [1, 0]^\\top$ and $\\varphi(t) = [1, 1]^\\top$ for $t \\ge 2$, yielding\n$$\\left(\\sum_{t=1}^N \\varphi(t)\\varphi^\\top(t)\\right)^{-1} = \\begin{bmatrix} N & N-1 \\\\ N-1 & N-1 \\end{bmatrix}^{-1} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{N}{N-1} \\end{bmatrix}$$\nand LS estimates $\\hat{b}_1 = y(1)$, $\\hat{b}_2 = -y(1) + \\frac{1}{N-1}\\sum_{t=2}^N y(t)$. Which statement accurately describes the asymptotic properties of $\\hat{b}_1$, $\\hat{b}_2$, and the static gain estimate $\\hat{b}_1 + \\hat{b}_2$ as $N \\to \\infty$?",
