    "explanation": "From `SI_rexam2020.pdf` (Problem 4, pp. 3, 6–7):\n1. Since $\\Phi^\\top\\Phi = \\begin{bmatrix} N & N-1 \\\\ N-1 & N-1 \\end{bmatrix}$ is invertible for all $N \\ge 2$ and $\\mathbb{E}[e(t)] = 0$, the LS estimator $\\hat{\\theta} = [\\hat{b}_1, \\hat{b}_2]^\\top$ is unbiased.\n2. Its covariance matrix is $\\operatorname{cov}(\\hat{\\theta}) = \\sigma^2(\\Phi^\\top\\Phi)^{-1} = \\sigma^2\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{N}{N-1} \\end{bmatrix}$, so $\\operatorname{Var}(\\hat{b}_1) = \\sigma^2$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(\\hat{b}_2) = \\sigma^2\\frac{N}{N-1} \\to \\sigma^2$ as $N \\to \\infty$. Neither individual parameter estimate is consistent!\n3. However, adding the two estimates cancels $y(1)$:\n$$\\hat{b}_1 + \\hat{b}_2 = \\frac{1}{N-1}\\sum_{t=2}^N y(t) = b_1^o + b_2^o + \\frac{1}{N-1}\\sum_{t=2}^N e(t),$$\nwhich is an unbiased and consistent estimator of the static gain $b_1^o + b_2^o$ with variance $\\operatorname{Var}(\\hat{b}_1 + \\hat{b}_2) = \\frac{\\sigma^2}{N-1} \\to 0$ as $N \\to \\infty$."
