    "explanation": "With $u(t) = -2y(t) + v(t)$, substituting into the system equation gives the closed-loop output:\n$$y(t) = 2y(t-1) + u(t-1) + e(t) = 2y(t-1) - 2y(t-1) + v(t-1) + e(t) = v(t-1) + e(t).$$\nSince $v(t)$ is white noise independent of $e(t)$, $v(t)$ is uncorrelated with $y(t)$. Thus:\n$$\\mathbb{E}[y(t-1)u(t-1)] = \\mathbb{E}[y(t)(-2y(t) + v(t))] = -2\\lambda_y,$$\n$$\\mathbb{E}[u^2(t-1)] = \\mathbb{E}[(-2y(t) + v(t))^2] = 4\\lambda_y + \\lambda_v.$$\nHence, the regression covariance matrix is:\n$$\\mathbb{E}[\\varphi(t)\\varphi^\\top(t)] = \\begin{bmatrix} \\lambda_y & 2\\lambda_y \\\\ 2\\lambda_y & 4\\lambda_y + \\lambda_v \\end{bmatrix},$$\nwhich has determinant $\\lambda_y(4\\lambda_y + \\lambda_v) - 4\\lambda_y^2 = \\lambda_y \\lambda_v > 0$, and inverse:\n$$\\mathbb{E}[\\varphi(t)\\varphi^\\top(t)]^{-1} = \\frac{1}{\\lambda_y \\lambda_v} \\begin{bmatrix} 4\\lambda_y + \\lambda_v & -2\\lambda_y \\\\ -2\\lambda_y & \\lambda_y \\end{bmatrix}.$$\nFurthermore, since $y(t) = v(t-1) + e(t)$ is white noise, $\\mathbb{E}[y(t)y(t-1)] = 0$, while $\\mathbb{E}[y(t)u(t-1)] = \\mathbb{E}[(v(t-1)+e(t))(-2y(t-1)+v(t-1))] = \\lambda_v$. Multiplying gives the asymptotic limit:\n$$\\hat{\\theta} \\to \\frac{1}{\\lambda_y \\lambda_v} \\begin{bmatrix} 4\\lambda_y + \\lambda_v & -2\\lambda_y \\\\ -2\\lambda_y & \\lambda_y \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} -\\mathbb{E}[y(t)y(t-1)] \\\\ \\mathbb{E}[y(t)u(t-1)] \\end{bmatrix} = \\frac{1}{\\lambda_y \\lambda_v} \\begin{bmatrix} 4\\lambda_y + \\lambda_v & -2\\lambda_y \\\\ -2\\lambda_y & \\lambda_y \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ \\lambda_v \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\theta_o.$$"
